{
  "_doc": "Background swap: keep the product's real pixels, replace only the scene behind it. SAM 3 (node 30) segments the subject named by the subject phrase; AILab_SDMatte (50) refines that into a matte; the contour is smoothed and thresholded at 0.75 (54) so no sliver of background stays attached; InvertMask (32) + GrowMask 6 (31) make the background region, grown slightly into the subject. Qwen-Image 2.1 inpaints only that region from the scene prompt (grey-filled reference, 40 steps, denoise 1.0), the decode is scaled back to the original size (60/61), and the ORIGINAL subject is composited back over it through a lightly feathered matte (54 -> 56 -> 57) so the real subject edge is preserved and only the background is generated. Filled per request: the image (4), the subject phrase (30), the scene prompt and negative_prompt (6), the seed (3).",
